<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Fill a three-set Venn diagram</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\({@N@}\) learners at a school in {@town@} were asked which of three clubs they belong to: {@c1@} (\({@L1@}\)), {@c2@} (\({@L2@}\)) and {@c3@} (\({@L3@}\)).</p><p>\({@nA@}\) belong to {@c1@}, \({@nB@}\) to {@c2@} and \({@nC@}\) to {@c3@}. \({@nAB@}\) belong to {@c1@} and {@c2@}, \({@nAC@}\) to {@c1@} and {@c3@}, and \({@nBC@}\) to {@c2@} and {@c3@}; \({@c@}\) belong to all three.</p><p>(a) How many belong to {@c1@} only? [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) How many belong to exactly two clubs? [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) How many belong to none of the three? [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Fill the region that belongs to the most sets first, then work outwards.</p><ol><li><p>Centre: \({@c@}\) belong to all three.</p></li><li><p>Exactly two: {@c1@} and {@c2@} only \({@nAB@} - {@c@} = {@r2@}\); {@c1@} and {@c3@} only \({@nAC@} - {@c@} = {@r4@}\); {@c2@} and {@c3@} only \({@nBC@} - {@c@} = {@r6@}\).</p></li><li><p>Only one: {@c1@} only \({@nA@} - {@r2@} - {@r4@} - {@c@} = {@r1@}\); {@c2@} only \({@nB@} - {@r2@} - {@r6@} - {@c@} = {@r3@}\); {@c3@} only \({@nC@} - {@r4@} - {@r6@} - {@c@} = {@r7@}\).</p></li><li><p>None: the seven inner regions add up to \({@N-r8@}\), so none \(= {@N@} - {@N-r8@} = {@r8@}\).</p></li><li><p>Check: {@c1@} \({@r1@} + {@r2@} + {@r4@} + {@c@} = {@nA@}\), and the same for the other two sets.</p></li></ol><p>(a) {@c1@} only: \({@r1@}\). (b) Exactly two: \({@r2@} + {@r4@} + {@r6@} = {@two@}\). (c) None: \({@r8@}\).</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Venn diagram of the club counts: {@L1@} only {@r1@}, {@L1@} and {@L2@} only {@r2@}, {@L2@} only {@r3@}, {@L1@} and {@L3@} only {@r4@}, all three {@r5@}, {@L2@} and {@L3@} only {@r6@}, {@L3@} only {@r7@}, none {@r8@}">
[[jsxgraph width="420px" height="300px"]]
(function () {
  var lab = {#labs#}, txt = {#[r1,r2,r3,r4,r5,r6,r7,r8]#}, circ = false, shd = {#[]#};
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [-4.2, 3, 4.2, -3], axis: false, grid: false, keepaspectratio: true,
      showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  var three = (lab.length === 3), i, j;
  var C2 = [[-1, 0, 1.7], [1, 0, 1.7]], C3 = [[-0.85, 0.55, 1.55], [0.85, 0.55, 1.55], [0, -0.9, 1.55]];
  var CC = three ? C3 : C2;
  var P2 = [[-1.8, 0], [0, 0], [1.8, 0], [-3.5, -2.4]];
  var P3 = [[-1.6, 1.0], [0, 1.35], [1.6, 1.0], [-1.05, -0.55], [0, 0.05], [1.05, -0.55], [0, -1.85], [-3.5, -2.5]];
  var PP = three ? P3 : P2;
  var L2 = [[-2.6, 1.6], [2.6, 1.6]], L3 = [[-2.35, 2.05], [2.35, 2.05], [1.55, -2.35]];
  var LL = three ? L3 : L2;
  function inC(k, x, y) { var c = CC[k]; return (x - c[0]) * (x - c[0]) + (y - c[1]) * (y - c[1]) < c[2] * c[2]; }
  function region(x, y) {
    if (x < -4 || x > 4 || y < -2.8 || y > 2.8) { return 0; }
    if (!three) { var a = inC(0, x, y), bb = inC(1, x, y); return a ? (bb ? 2 : 1) : (bb ? 3 : 4); }
    var code = (inC(0, x, y) ? 1 : 0) + (inC(1, x, y) ? 2 : 0) + (inC(2, x, y) ? 4 : 0);
    return [8, 1, 3, 2, 7, 4, 6, 5][code];
  }
